<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $434 mln in July 23 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $434 mln in July 23 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $434 million to $47,233 million in the week ended July 23, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $434 million to $47,512 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $196 million to $871,847 million.</p>
<p>(( -- Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
